>Always worked for me. There seems to be some test in the code to let
it land on a dry spot.

Did a source dive, and I *think* you are right.  method goodpos() in
teleport.c has a while loop that checks to ensure there's a good
position to teleport to, and unless the "ignorewater" flag is set it
will not allow a monster, an object, or a player to teleport into water
or solid rock.

Pity, really.  I recall some people complaining on this group that
Nethack is too easy. That would be an easy way to make this game harder
-- rewrite the loop so that uncontrolled teleport by player or by
monster is NOT safe.   You could wind up ANYWHERE in the level,
including in solid rock (instadeath), in water (instadeath if not
equipped for water), in lava (you get the idea) ... it'd change the
current teleport scroll from a near-certain escape hatch to a hazardous
gambit that is as likely to kill you as save you.

I recall a game from the 80s called "Zoarre" not unlike nethack where
teleport was handled just that way. Lethal, lethal game.

